### Static launcher (`--format launcher`)

Context word 408 = 4 (ADR 0371 step 4; 2 is `--format packed`), built from
`tools/static_launcher.kotoba`. The runtime text is `xs-rt-core` followed by
`xs-rt-launch` instead of the standard start (`xs-rt-start`); static and runner
images are `xs-rt-core` + `xs-rt-start`, the same bytes as before the split.
Command line: `WALL ALLOW GRANT PROVIDER [ARG ...] -- GUEST [ARG ...]`: WALL
1..86400 seconds; ALLOW is the guest's `KEXE_ALLOW` (ids 0..255 or `-`, at most
1024 bytes); GRANT and PROVIDER are both `-` or both paths, and ALLOW names
wire 42 exactly when a provider is given. Refusals print one line
`kexe-launcher: <reason>[: guest|provider|grant|launcher image]` on stderr
and exit 2 (usage, WALL, ALLOW) or 1 (an input that cannot be read, is empty
or over its bound (images 256 MiB, grant 1 MiB), cannot be sealed, a pipe or
process that cannot be made, a child that cannot be executed, stdio not open,
the filter, the wait); started children are killed and reaped first.
Each input is read once into a memfd (MFD_CLOEXEC|MFD_ALLOW_SEALING) while
SHA-256 is computed, then sealed (F_SEAL_SEAL|SHRINK|GROW|WRITE) and rewound;
`/proc/self/exe` is hashed as the launcher image. Children are `clone(SIGCHLD)`
forks: PR_SET_PDEATHSIG SIGKILL (and exit 127 if the parent changed), the
status pipe and image to fds 110/111 and the sources to 100.. (close-on-exec),
`close_range` 3..99 and 112.. (else close one by one), the sources onto their
targets, an empty signal mask, PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS, then
`execveat(111, "", argv, envp, AT_EMPTY_PATH)`; a failure writes its stage
byte (1 dup, 2 target, 3 no_new_privs, 4 exec) on the close-on-exec status
pipe, whose end of file means the exec happened. The provider (argv:
PROVIDER and its ARGs; the environment MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE=true
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=~all~ and nothing else) gets fd 0 requests, 1 answers,
2 the launcher's stderr, 3 the grant memfd, 4 its report pipe; the guest
(argv: GUEST and its ARGs) gets 0 the launcher's stdin, 1 a pipe to the
launcher, 2 the launcher's stderr, and with a provider 3 requests and
4 answers, and the environment `KEXE_ALLOW=ALLOW`, `KEXE_STRUCTURED_REPORT=1`,
`KEXE_WALL_SECONDS=WALL`, `KEXE_CAP_RESOURCES_42=3,4` (with a provider) plus
the launcher's own `KEXE_FUEL`, `KEXE_STACK_BYTES`, `KEXE_CPU_SECONDS`,
`KEXE_SECCOMP`, `KEXE_CAP_RESOURCES_35`, `KEXE_ARENA_USE` and
`KEXE_SANDBOX_PROBE` when set. After both have executed the launcher closes
every child end, sets RLIMIT_STACK 1 MiB (pre-touched, as the standard start
does), RLIMIT_CORE 0 and RLIMIT_AS 64 MiB, ignores SIGPIPE and
installs its filter: the base set plus read, close, ppoll, wait4 and kill
(`KEXE_SECCOMP=if-available` as for images). It then `ppoll`s the guest's
stdout, the provider's report and both pidfds (pidfd_open, Linux 5.3; no
